      "tr": "NumPy'de `x.std()` `n`'e böler; `x.std(ddof=1)` `n - 1`'e.",
      "en": "In NumPy `x.std()` divides by `n`; `x.std(ddof=1)` by `n - 1`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Yalnızca paydayı değiştir: `x.std(ddof=1)`.",
      "en": "Change only the denominator: `x.std(ddof=1)`."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef z_scores(values):\n    x = np.array(values, dtype=float)\n    z = (x - x.mean()) / x.std(ddof=1)\n    return [round(float(v), 2) for v in z]\n\n\nprint(z_scores([2, 4, 4, 5, 7, 9]))\nprint(z_scores([10, 20, 30]))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef z_scores(values):\n    x = np.array(values, dtype=float)\n    z = (x - x.mean()) / x.std(ddof=1)\n    return [round(float(v), 2) for v in z]\n\n\nprint(z_scores([2, 4, 4, 5, 7, 9]))\nprint(z_scores([10, 20, 30]))\n```"
    }
